{
  "format": "rerail.policy/v1",
  "id": "ruff-sim223-expr-and-false",
  "revision": 1,
  "mode": "steer",
  "description": "Port of Ruff's SIM223 (expr-and-false), `is_short_circuit` in flake8_simplify/rules/ast_bool_op.rs:736. Over the values of one `and` run (tree-sitter nests them to the left; parentheses start a new run), a value whose truthiness is unknown is skipped when the run is not in a boolean test, or when it has a side effect (`contains_effect`). The first value that is not skipped and is falsy (`False`, `None`, zero, an empty literal, ...), or whose successor is, triggers; the finding starts at the value after the last skipped value before it (the whole expression when none), as Ruff's `furthest`. Truthiness follows `Truthiness::from_expr`, including f-string emptiness and `list(...)`-style calls. The finding spans that value only; Ruff's range runs to the end of the expression.",
  "scope": {
    "include": [
      "**/*"
    ],
    "exclude": []
  },
  "clauses": [
    {
      "id": "expr-and-false",
      "forbid": {
        "ast": {
          "language": "python",
